    "title": "Democrats Establish 2028 Primary Calendar Prioritizing Diverse States",
    "category": "Politics",
    "topic_label": "2028 Presidential Primary",
    "summary": "The Democratic National Committee has finalized the 2028 presidential primary calendar, designating South Carolina as the first state to vote on January 22, 2028. This new lineup shifts the traditional early voting state of Iowa to a later position and emphasizes the importance of Black and Latino voters, as well as union members, in the selection of the party's nominee. Following South Carolina, Nevada will hold its primary on February 1, 2028.",
